usage:
  factory where [<project-slug>]            print this project's factory paths as JSON
  factory init [<repo-path>]                set up the factory home and register a repo
  factory claim <factory-dir> <feature-slug> <project-slug>
                                            allocate a job id, its folder, and its claim, print the id
  factory board <factory-dir> <job-id>      apply a JSON merge patch (stdin) to one job; a new id must
                                            look like 003-rate-limiting
  factory next                              claim the first backlog line this device can run,
                                            print its id, project, and feature as JSON
  factory backlog add "<slug>: <feature>" [--context <file>]
                                            append a line to the backlog, with the file's reasons,
                                            recommendation, and questions indented under it
  factory backlog rework <job-id>           read a reworded feature on stdin, append it as
                                            (rework-of <job-id>), and close that rework job
  factory backlog decide <key> <approve|deny|rework> [--answers <file>] [--notes-file <file>]
                      --chat-file <file>
                                            make the dashboard's backlog decision from a person's chat
                                            message, print the job as JSON
  factory lesson <slug>/<job-id> --fact-file <file> [--why-file <file>]
                                            append a lesson to the project's notes.md under the retro caps,
                                            or queue it as a lesson card
  factory triage replay <project-slug> [--threshold N] [--rules-file PATH]
                                            score a threshold against past human backlog decisions, print JSON
  factory bench score <cases-file> <arm-folder>...
                                            score saved reviewer runs against labeled past defects, print JSON
                                            (offline)
  factory bench replay <cases-file> <arm-folder> --role <reviewer> [--model <model>]
                                            run a reviewer on each case at its head, write review and run.json
                                            for bench score
  factory bench cases <project-slug>
                                            draft reviewer-benchmark cases from reverted or reworked jobs, print JSON
  factory ideas [--limit N] [--max-inflight N] [--project <slug>]
                                            claim the oldest ideas this device can run, print them as JSON
                                            (exit 3 when none are runnable or the cap is full)
  factory routes pick|list|limit <name> [--minutes N]|clear <name>
                                            this host's dispatch routes from routes.md; pick prints
                                            the first not marked limited (exit 3 when all are)
  factory experiment report <name>          print per-arm outcome metrics for one owner-model
                                            experiment as JSON (read-only)
  factory trial settle                      keep, revert, supersede or time out each open retro
                                            stage-note trial; 2 reverts pause a project's trials
  factory trial resume <slug> <reason>      a person, or an agent a person asked, clears that pause
  factory unclaim <job-id>                  release this session's claim on an idea, so it waits again
  factory deny-notes <job-id> [done]      print a denied job's unread notes wrapped as data, or mark them read
  factory pickup [--dry-run] [--triage-now] [--limit N] [--max-inflight N]
                                            claim and launch runnable ideas for the projects whose
                                            pipeline lists this host, through launchers.json; silent
                                            when there is nothing to do. The backlog triage sweep
                                            runs at most every 30 minutes; --triage-now runs it now
  factory pickup setup [--install]          check every pickup prerequisite on this host and print each fix; --install writes and loads the 5 minute timer
  factory catch-up                          bring this host to origin's skill, pickup timer and Worker, backing up first
  factory host pair <id> <code>             pair this device with a host added in Settings and set
                                            device: <id> in config.md
  factory pipeline <project-slug> [--board]
                                            print the project's effective pipeline configuration as JSON,
                                            with stage notes wrapped as operator-preferences data;
                                            --board prints only the one-line board patch {"pipeline": <versions>}
  factory documents <project-slug>          write the project's notes, decisions and runbook, wrapped as
                                            operator-preferences data, to projects/<slug>.documents.md
                                            and print its path
  factory prompt <project-slug>/<job-id> <role> [--round N] [--port P] [--out <path>]
                                            print a role's full agent prompt (spec, build, review-security,
                                            review-ux, review-ui, review-code, approve), or write it to
                                            <path> with mode 600 and print the path
  factory wait <project-slug>/<job-id> <artifact>... [--timeout S] [--hold]
                                            print each finished job file's first line, checking once a
                                            second for up to S seconds (default 60); exit 3 while one is
                                            missing, 5 while one has no valid first line; --hold runs
                                            hold first to refresh this session's claim
  factory watch <project-slug>/<job-id> [<artifact>...] [--pr] [--timeout S]
                                            print one JSON line when every job file has a valid first
                                            line, one keeps an invalid first line, --pr's next leaves
                                            wait, or S seconds pass (default and max 540); runs hold first
                                            when a session tag is set
  factory round-wait <project-slug>/<job-id> <round> [--timeout S]
                                            block until all four review files of round N have a verdict
                                            line, write each verdict to the board's rounds entry as it
                                            lands, print one JSON line (default and max 540 seconds); runs
                                            hold first
  factory verdict <project-slug>/<job-id> <round> <reviewer> <verdict>
                                            set one reviewer's verdict in the board's rounds entry, print it
                                            as JSON
  factory checks <project-slug>/<job-id> [--timeout S]
                                            print the job PR's checks as <bucket> <name> once none is
                                            pending, checking every 10 seconds for up to S seconds
                                            (default 300); no checks after 120 seconds exits 0, a failing
                                            check 1, pending at the deadline 3, a bad pr 4, a gh problem 5, an escalated job 7
  factory pr-state <project-slug>/<job-id> [--wait S]
                                            print one JSON reading of the job PR for /factory babysit:
                                            pr, state, review, checks, queued, conflict, items, capped,
                                            rearm, behind and next; --wait
                                            re-reads every 30 seconds for up to S seconds (1 to 600) while
                                            next is wait; a bad pr exits 4, a gh problem 5
  factory pr-handled <project-slug>/<job-id> [--rearm] <sig>...
                                            record that babysit acted on up to 32 pr-state item signatures:
                                            add 1 to each count in the job's handled field, or with --rearm
                                            drop them; keeps the newest 32 and prints one JSON line of id
                                            and handled; a bad sig exits 2, another session's claim 6
  factory pr-queue <project-slug>/<job-id>
                                            print whether GitHub queued the job PR, by the enqueue mutation first, else merge-async:
                                            one JSON line of pr, status and detail; enqueued exits 0,
                                            failed or refused 1, pending after 120 seconds 3, a bad or
                                            stacked pr 4, a gh problem 5
  factory pr-merge <project-slug>/<job-id>
                                            check the job PR can merge, then merge it pinned to the head
                                            checks passed, or queue it when the repo has a merge queue: one
                                            JSON line of pr, status and detail; merged or enqueued exits 0,
                                            blocked, draft or refused 1, behind, unknown or a head checks
                                            did not pass 3, a bad or stacked pr 4, a gh problem 5, a
                                            conflict 6, an escalated job 7, an autonomy hold 8
  factory batch <project-slug>/<job-id> [<idea-id> ...]     list ideas to batch into a job at spec, or attach up to 20 of them
  factory stack <project-slug>/<job-id> <rider-id>     mark one rider of a job at spec to ship as a PR stacked on the job's PR
  factory escalation <project-slug>/<job-id> <round>
                                            ask whether a review round's CHANGES findings need a person,
                                            print one JSON verdict
  factory repeats <project-slug>/<job-id> <round>
                                            compare a review round's CHANGES signatures with every earlier round, print one JSON verdict
                                              and flag files changed in each of the last 3 fix rounds
  factory review-plan <project-slug>/<job-id> <round>
                                            skip the ux and ui reviews of a round that changes nothing a person sees, print one JSON plan
  factory review-floor <project-slug>/<job-id>
                                            record the review tier and full-review flag so a later edit cannot lower them
  factory pre-review <project-slug>/<job-id>
                                            run the base branch's .factory/checks.json in the job
                                            worktree, write pre-review.md, print one JSON line; FAIL exits 1
  factory build-landed <project-slug>/<job-id>
                                            hold the job, print the latest build.md run's first line, push factory/<id> and the job folder
  factory grounding <project-slug>/<job-id> <round>
                                            check each path:line a round's reviews cite, write
                                            round-N/grounding.md and the round's unverified list; flags only
  factory stop <worktree>                   stop processes running out of a worktree
  factory cleanup <project-slug>/<job-id>
                                            stop the job's processes, remove its worktree and merged
                                            branch without forcing, print what was left as JSON
  factory clean <project-slug>/<job-id> node_modules | scratch <name> | temp
                                            remove the job worktree's git-ignored node_modules folders, or
                                            its .context/<name> scratch folder, or the job's temp folder
                                            under the system temp root, never through a link; print
                                            what was removed and left as JSON
  factory archive-workspace <project-slug>/<job-id> [--check]
                                            archive this session's Paseo worktree workspace and agent once
                                            the job is merged or closed, whatever its git state; print
                                            leftovers as JSON
                                            (--check: print only)
  factory orphans                           list factory branches, open PRs, worktrees and Paseo workspaces
                                            that no open board job owns, with a reason each, as JSON;
                                            never removes anything
  factory push <project-slug>[/<job-id>] upload a project file, or a job's changed markdown and images, to R2
  factory pull <project-slug>[/<job-id>] download a project, or a job's changed markdown and images from R2
  factory idea-images <project-slug>/<job-id>
                                            materialize a job's pasted images and their
                                            Markdown into the job folder, then push them
  factory idea-files <project-slug>/<job-id>
                                            fetch a job's attached files into the job folder
                                            for the spec prompt, without pushing them
  factory sync [<project-slug>]             pull every active job of one project
                                            or of all projects, skipping merged
                                            and closed jobs
  factory tracer sync [<project-slug>[/<job-id>]]
                                            mirror jobs into Tracer for projects listed in tracer.json
  factory hold <project-slug>/<job-id> [take|released]
                                            claim a job for this session, then pull it and print the seconds since the job started;
                                            released also verifies the pulled job artifacts
                                            against R2 before the resume may dispatch work
  factory handoff <project-slug>/<job-id>
                                            publish a checkpoint and release this session's claim
  factory worktree <project-slug>/<job-id>
                                            create or fast-forward the job's worktree from origin
  factory start <job-id>                    promote an idea: job, where, hold, sync, spec board patch,
                                            worktree, documents and batch candidates in one call
  factory job <job-id>                      print one job's board entry as JSON
  factory inbox                             print the dashboard Inbox count across all projects and
                                            the jobs waiting on a person as JSON
  factory builds <project-slug>             print the project's build queue and in-flight jobs as JSON
  factory stuck [--limit N]                 claim up to N (default 1) jobs a dead session left mid-loop,
                                            print them as JSON for the resume schedule
  factory autonomy status|pause|resume|allow <slug>|deny <slug>|self <slug>|restore <slug> <class>|promote <slug> <class>
                                            show or change the explorer kill switch and allowlist;
                                            resume and allow need a human typing at a terminal
  factory autonomy report [<project-slug>]     recommend which project and job classes may automerge; writes nothing
  factory autonomy restore <project-slug> internal|visible     lift an earned-autonomy hold; a human types at a terminal
  factory autonomy promote <project-slug> internal|visible     lift a hold the class has earned; a human types at a terminal
  factory halt status | halt set --reason <text>
                                            show or set the global stop flag that pickup, its takeover
                                            and stuck honor; only a signed-in person clears it
  factory suggest admit <file>              turn an explorer's suggestions file into idea cards that
                                            wait on a human (exit 3 when paused or none admitted)
  factory suggest approve <job-id> <A|B|C> [--chat-file <file>]
                                            a human at a terminal approves one option of such a card,
                                            or --chat-file records a person's chat message instead
  factory control <job-id> <prioritize|unprioritize|pause|resume|babysit|rerun> --chat-file <file>
  factory control <job-id> move <host> --chat-file <file>
  factory control <job-id> close --reason-file <file> --chat-file <file>
                                            make the dashboard's Prioritize, Remove priority, Pause,
                                            Resume, Babysit PR, Move, Rerun or Close from a person's
                                            chat message, print the result as JSON
  factory needs answer <job-id> --answers <file> --chat-file <file>
                                            submit a person's chat answers to a job's needs.md form
                                            with the dashboard's writes, print the result as JSON
  factory explore <slug> [done <run>]      snapshot an allowlisted project for a read-only explorer, or remove that snapshot
  factory retro digest [--days N]           print one redacted JSON line per Claude Code main session
                                            from the last N days (default 1)
  factory retro push                        upload that digest (last day) to retro/<device>/<local date>.jsonl
  factory retro pull YYYY-MM-DD             print every host's pushed digest for that date
  factory retro aggregate [--days N]        pull every host's digest for the last N days (default 7, at most 30) into retro/<run>/
  factory retro admit <run>                 check retro/<run>/reply.json, write findings.md, add its cards to the backlog
  factory audit <job-id>                    list this host's tool calls in the job's worktree, risky ones flagged
  factory audit push <job-id>               upload this host's audit rows to audit/<job-id>/<device>.jsonl
  factory usage <project-slug>/<job-id>     sum this host's transcript tokens for the job by model
  factory usage record <project-slug>/<job-id>
                                            write those totals to the board job under tokens.<device>
  factory outcomes [record] [<project-slug>]
                                            sort jobs merged in the last 90 days into held, reworked or reverted;
                                            record writes outcome
  factory with-cloudflare -- <command> [<arg>...]
                                            run one command with the CLOUDFLARE_* keys of this home's .env
                                            in its environment; prints no value
  factory agent record <project-slug>/<job-id> <role> <harness> <via> <model> [<effort>] [--paseo-agent <agent-id>]
                                            append one row to the job's agents, after checking this
                                            session holds the claim, and print it as JSON
  factory agent report [<project-slug>]     count every job's agents rows by stage, role, harness, via,
                                            model and effort, as a plain-text table

claim, next, hold, handoff, board, ideas, and stuck take --session <tag> (or
FACTORY_SESSION). A session without one gets a new tag from claim, next, or hold,
printed on stderr; handoff requires the session tag that holds the job. stuck instead
gives each job it claims its own tag, in its JSON.

Exit codes: 2 bad usage, 3 nothing in the backlog (or no idea, or nothing stuck) this
device can run, 4 not found, 5 Worker or network failure, 6 another session holds the
job, R2 or origin moved under this device, local job artifacts do not match R2, or a
job path is a symlink or junction or cannot be inspected, or a pairing was refused, or
the checkout holds history origin's base does not descend from.

The board, backlog, and project files live in R2 behind the factory Worker at
`api_url` in config.md. Job folders and worktrees stay on this device.

